From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:23:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 44/49] Box hooks: extension work of a tiled task on each
 thread's own y lines

The tiled sweep (OPENEMS_TBLOCK) ran the extension hooks of a task as a
stage of its own in which every thread took whole x-lines. With tiles of
5 to 15 x-lines and 12 to 18 threads, one to five threads did all the
extension work while the others waited: at 30 M cells with a PML the
tiled sweep ran at 0.26 to 0.79 of the fused sweep.

Engine_Extension gets BOX_HOOKS and six hooks that take an x range and a
y range (Do{Pre,Post}{Voltage,Current}UpdatesBox, Apply2{Voltages,Current}Box).
When every extension with a hook declares them, a tiled task runs
Pre box hooks, the update, Post and Apply box hooks on the thread's own
y lines behind one barrier; otherwise the hook stages stay (the log line
says which and why). OPENEMS_TBLOCK_BOX=0 keeps the hook stages.

Box hooks in this commit: UPML (f4vector rows, scalar rows, y-vector
groups; a group cut by the y range runs its own lanes), excitation and
lumped RLC (index lists filtered by the box), steady-state detection
(row copies, the last thread evaluates).

Results are bit-identical to the hook stages and to the fused sweep
(raw fields, probes, steady-state stop step). Mac Studio (M5 Max),
30 M cells with a PML, 18 threads: tiled with box hooks 1.15 to 1.28
times the fused sweep, with hook stages 0.32. The tiled sweep stays
opt-in. The default path does not change: 38 of 38 hot functions have
the same machine code as before.

